### Push Notifications API
### Base URL: http://localhost:5000/api

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@token = your_jwt_token_here
@employeeToken = your_employee_jwt_token_here

############################################################
# DEVICE REGISTRATION
############################################################

### Register Device for Push Notifications
# Register a device to receive push notifications
# Requires: User or Employee authentication
# Body Parameters:
#   - platform: Device platform ('web', 'android', 'ios') (required)
#   - deviceId: Unique device identifier (required)
#   - token: Push notification token (required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "android",
  "deviceId": "device-unique-id-123",
  "token": "fcm-token-or-apns-token-here"
}

### Register Web Device
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "web",
  "deviceId": "web-device-id-456",
  "token": "web-push-token-here"
}

### Register iOS Device
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "ios",
  "deviceId": "ios-device-id-789",
  "token": "apns-token-here"
}

############################################################
# DEVICE REVOCATION
############################################################

### Revoke Device Registration
# Remove a device from receiving push notifications
# Requires: User or Employee authentication
# Body Parameters:
#   - platform: Device platform ('web', 'android', 'ios') (required)
#   - deviceId: Unique device identifier (required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "platform": "android",
  "deviceId": "device-unique-id-123"
}

############################################################
# TEST PUSH NOTIFICATION
############################################################

### Send Test Push Notification
# Send a test push notification to the authenticated user/employee
# Requires: User or Employee authentication
# Body Parameters:
#   - title: Notification title (required)
#   - body: Notification body (required)
#   - source_event_key: Optional source event key
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Notification",
  "body": "This is a test push notification",
  "source_event_key": "test:notification:2026-02-14"
}

############################################################
# SEND NOTIFICATION (EMPLOYEE ONLY)
############################################################

### Send Notification to Specific Users/Employees
# Send a notification to specific users or employees by their IDs
# Requires: Employee authentication
# Body Parameters:
#   - userIds: Array of user IDs (optional)
#   - employeeIds: Array of employee IDs (optional)
#   - type: Notification type (required)
#   - title: Notification title (required)
#   - body: Notification body (required)
#   - source_event_key: Optional source event key
#   - payload: Optional payload object
#   - actions: Optional actions array (max 2)
#   - targets: Optional platform targets array
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/notify
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userIds": [
    "0ed09547-b0bc-43e7-af16-4cfd56aca6c0",
    "7f040b8f-6111-4d4f-a544-acdba48509ff"
  ],
  "type": "custom_notification",
  "title": "Custom Notification",
  "body": "This is a custom notification sent to specific users",
  "source_event_key": "custom:notification:2026-02-14",
  "payload": {
    "customData": "value"
  }
}

### Send Notification to Employees Only
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/notify
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeIds": [
    "employee-uuid-1",
    "employee-uuid-2"
  ],
  "type": "task_assignment",
  "title": "New Task",
  "body": "You have been assigned a new task",
  "source_event_key": "task:assigned:2026-02-14"
}

############################################################
# BROADCAST NOTIFICATIONS (EMPLOYEE ONLY)
############################################################

### Send Notification to All Clients
# Send a notification to all clients (users with mode='client')
# Requires: Employee authentication
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/broadcast
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetType": "clients",
  "type": "announcement",
  "title": "New Feature Available",
  "body": "We've just released a new feature that you might find useful!",
  "sourceEventKey": "announcement:new-feature:2026-02-14",
  "payload": {
    "featureId": "feature-123",
    "link": "/features/new-feature"
  },
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "view",
      "title": "View Feature",
      "url": "/features/new-feature"
    }
  ]
}

### Send Notification to All Employees
# Send a notification to all active employees
# Requires: Employee authentication
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/broadcast
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetType": "employees",
  "type": "system_alert",
  "title": "System Maintenance",
  "body": "Scheduled maintenance will occur tonight from 2 AM to 4 AM.",
  "sourceEventKey": "system:maintenance:2026-02-14"
}

### Send Notification to Specific Users
# Send a notification to specific users by their IDs
# Requires: Employee authentication
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/broadcast
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetType": "specific",
  "userIds": [
    "0ed09547-b0bc-43e7-af16-4cfd56aca6c0",
    "7f040b8f-6111-4d4f-a544-acdba48509ff"
  ],
  "type": "personal_message",
  "title": "Important Update",
  "body": "You have an important update regarding your account.",
  "sourceEventKey": "personal:update:2026-02-14"
}

### Send Notification to Specific Employees
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/broadcast
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetType": "specific",
  "employeeIds": [
    "employee-uuid-1",
    "employee-uuid-2"
  ],
  "type": "task_assignment",
  "title": "New Task Assigned",
  "body": "You have been assigned a new task. Please review it.",
  "sourceEventKey": "task:assigned:2026-02-14"
}

### Send Notification with Platform Targets
# Send notification only to specific platforms
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/broadcast
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetType": "clients",
  "type": "mobile_only_announcement",
  "title": "Mobile App Update",
  "body": "A new version of our mobile app is available!",
  "targets": ["android", "ios"],
  "sourceEventKey": "mobile:update:2026-02-14"
}

############################################################
# RESPONSE FORMATS
############################################################

### Success Response - Register Device (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "data": {
#     "platform": "android",
#     "deviceId": "device-unique-id-123",
#     "endpointArn": "arn:aws:sns:region:account:endpoint/GCM/..."
#   }
# }

### Success Response - Test Push (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "data": {
#     "enqueued": 1,
#     "skipped": 0
#   }
# }

### Success Response - Notify (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "data": {
#     "enqueued": 2,
#     "skipped": 0
#   }
# }

### Success Response - Broadcast to Clients (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Notifications sent successfully",
#   "data": {
#     "targetType": "clients",
#     "totalRecipients": 150,
#     "userCount": 150,
#     "employeeCount": 0,
#     "enqueued": 148,
#     "skipped": 2
#   }
# }

### Success Response - Broadcast to Employees (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Notifications sent successfully",
#   "data": {
#     "targetType": "employees",
#     "totalRecipients": 25,
#     "userCount": 0,
#     "employeeCount": 25,
#     "enqueued": 25,
#     "skipped": 0
#   }
# }

### Success Response - Broadcast to Specific Users (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Notifications sent successfully",
#   "data": {
#     "targetType": "specific",
#     "totalRecipients": 5,
#     "userCount": 3,
#     "employeeCount": 2,
#     "enqueued": 5,
#     "skipped": 0
#   }
# }

### Error Response - Missing Required Fields (400 Bad Request):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "targetType, type, title, and body are required"
# }

### Error Response - Invalid Target Type (400 Bad Request):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Invalid targetType. Must be 'clients', 'employees', or 'specific'"
# }

### Error Response - No Recipients (400 Bad Request):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "userIds or employeeIds are required when targetType is 'specific'"
# }

### Error Response - No Recipients Found (404 Not Found):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "No recipients found for the specified target type"
# }

### Error Response - Unauthorized (401 Unauthorized):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Unauthorized"
# }

### Error Response - Employee Access Required (401 Unauthorized):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Unauthorized - Employee access required"
# }

############################################################
# NOTES
############################################################

# 1. DEVICE REGISTRATION
#    - Users and employees can register their devices to receive push notifications
#    - Each device must have a unique deviceId per platform
#    - Platform must be one of: 'web', 'android', 'ios'
#    - Token format depends on platform (FCM for Android/Web, APNS for iOS)

# 2. TEST PUSH
#    - Sends a test notification to the authenticated user/employee
#    - Useful for testing push notification setup
#    - Available to both users and employees

# 3. NOTIFY ENDPOINT
#    - Employee-only endpoint
#    - Sends notifications to specific users/employees by IDs
#    - Requires userIds and/or employeeIds arrays

# 4. BROADCAST ENDPOINT
#    - Employee-only endpoint
#    - Can send to all clients, all employees, or specific users
#    - targetType options:
#      * 'clients': All users with mode='client'
#      * 'employees': All active employees
#      * 'specific': Specific users/employees by IDs
#    - Automatically finds recipients based on targetType

# 5. NOTIFICATION PROPERTIES
#    - type: Notification type identifier (e.g., 'announcement', 'task_assignment')
#    - title: Notification title (max 200 chars)
#    - body: Notification body (max 1000 chars)
#    - sourceEventKey: Optional key for deduplication
#    - payload: Optional JSON object with additional data
#    - actions: Optional array of action buttons (max 2)
#    - targets: Optional platform filter (e.g., ['web', 'android', 'ios'])

# 6. RATE LIMITING & DEDUPLICATION
#    - Notifications are automatically rate-limited (20 per minute per recipient)
#    - Duplicate notifications are prevented within 10 minutes
#    - Skipped notifications are due to rate limiting or deduplication

# 7. NOTIFICATION DELIVERY
#    - Notifications are queued via SQS
#    - Delivered asynchronously by push worker
#    - Status tracked in Notifications table (queued, sent, failed)

# 8. PLATFORM TARGETS
#    - Can filter notifications to specific platforms
#    - Useful for platform-specific announcements
#    - Options: 'web', 'android', 'ios'

# 9. ACTIONS
#    - Can include up to 2 action buttons
#    - Each action has: action, title, url
#    - Actions appear as buttons in the notification

# 10. AUTHENTICATION
#     - Device registration: User or Employee
#     - Test push: User or Employee
#     - Notify: Employee only
#     - Broadcast: Employee only
